Muscle mass is used to define strength, endurance, and performance. 
Muscle mass loss can affect a person's ability to complete daily activities (ADL).
The methods of confirming muscle mass are: 
    - Body Mass Index;
    - Computed Tomography;
    - Ultrasound Examination;
    - Magnetic Resonance Imaging;
    - Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry.
